{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l2knets3","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline","year":2011,"examDate":2011,"subject":"physics","chapter":"simple-harmonic-motion","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"simple-harmonic-motion","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pthe-phase-space-diagram-for-simple-harmonic-motion-is-a-c-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-ffvdpu4gg5j46wh1","content":"<p>The phase space diagram for simple harmonic motion is a circle centred at the origin. In the figure, the two circles represent the same oscillator but for different initial conditions, and E<sub>1</sub> and E<sub>2</sub> are the total mechanical energies respectively. Then</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l2lo8kea/d482c3f9-f9f4-40f3-9672-ce23350bc7d9/4baea220-c869-11ec-830c-7163a5cc8dc8/file-1l2lo8keb.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l2lo8kea/d482c3f9-f9f4-40f3-9672-ce23350bc7d9/4baea220-c869-11ec-830c-7163a5cc8dc8/file-1l2lo8keb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Simple Harmonic Motion Question 18 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l2lo8kea/d482c3f9-f9f4-40f3-9672-ce23350bc7d9/4baea220-c869-11ec-830c-7163a5cc8dc8/file-1l2lo8keb.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l2lo8kea/d482c3f9-f9f4-40f3-9672-ce23350bc7d9/4baea220-c869-11ec-830c-7163a5cc8dc8/file-1l2lo8keb.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l2lo8kea/d482c3f9-f9f4-40f3-9672-ce23350bc7d9/4baea220-c869-11ec-830c-7163a5cc8dc8/file-1l2lo8keb.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l2lo8kea/d482c3f9-f9f4-40f3-9672-ce23350bc7d9/4baea220-c869-11ec-830c-7163a5cc8dc8/file-1l2lo8keb.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l2lo8kea/d482c3f9-f9f4-40f3-9672-ce23350bc7d9/4baea220-c869-11ec-830c-7163a5cc8dc8/file-1l2lo8keb.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l2lo8kea/d482c3f9-f9f4-40f3-9672-ce23350bc7d9/4baea220-c869-11ec-830c-7163a5cc8dc8/file-1l2lo8keb.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"E<sub>1</sub> = <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.225ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.061ex\" height=\"2.398ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -960.5 1353 1060\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msqrt\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0,100.5)\"><use data-c=\"221A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-221A\"></use></g><g transform=\"translate(853,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"500\" height=\"60\" x=\"853\" y=\"840.5\"></rect></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>E<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"E<sub>1</sub> = 2E<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"E<sub>1</sub> = 4E<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"E<sub>1</sub> = 16E<sub>2</sub>"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<p>Energy of simple harmonic oscillator is</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10.404ex\" height=\"2.737ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.9 4598.7 1209.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D438\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D438\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1041.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2097.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2891.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D458\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D458\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(3412.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D434\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D434\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(783,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>where k is the force constant and A the amplitude of the oscillator. Since the oscillator is the same, the value of k is the same. Hence</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"11.333ex\" height=\"2.737ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.9 5009.2 1209.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D438\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D438\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(771,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1452.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></us